  <escalation>
    <trigger>This task is blocked on an owner decision and MUST NOT be started until it is answered. Starting it means choosing the answer.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <prompt>The `sprk_contactorganization` junction carries `sprk_enddate`, but `QueryActiveOrgIdsAsync` filters `statecode eq 0` ALONE. A membership ended by date but never deactivated still confers inherited access — via the org-grant term today, and via task 043's org-expansion term from now on.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, C#/.NET, the external access evaluator.</role>
  <goal>Whatever the owner decides, implemented so that BOTH fail directions stay closed — the additive terms cannot over-grant, and the ethical-wall veto cannot stop matching a subject it should wall.</goal>

  <owner-question status="UNDECIDED" put="2026-09-18">
    <part n="1">Should a date-ended but still state-active membership stop conferring access — i.e. should the additive terms bound on `sprk_enddate`?</part>
    <part n="2">If yes: should the ethical-wall veto keep matching that person anyway? The SAME query feeds an additive term (over-inclusion = over-GRANT, so a date bound is a tightening) AND the deny-veto subject (over-inclusion = a stricter wall, so the same date bound makes the wall match FEWER people — a fail-OPEN change to a veto). One query shape cannot be correct for both.</part>
    <part n="3">Should date-ended junction rows be backfilled or deactivated in data?</part>
    <recommendation>Yes to (1), no to (2) — a date-bounded variant for additive callers only, leaving the veto subject on statecode-only, which keeps both fail directions closed. (3) as a separate, audited data action.</recommendation>
  </owner-question>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="task 020">"Do not inherit the revoke's shape by default, because its fail direction is inverted relative to yours."</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 043">Today's safety is a DATA STATE, not a control: exposure is nil only because zero organisations hold a standing grant. One administrator ticking `sprk_standinggrant` arms an over-grant to every stale member.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">Fixing this NARROWS live org-grant inheritance — it changes who has access today. Treat the data change as its own audited action with a recorded before-state.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <notes>Register: `notes/defer-issues.md` § ISS-020. Related: tasks 020, 042, 043.</notes>
</task>
